## Context
spec-erg-v1.md currently covers both the file format and the binary commands.
Once 0089 moves command documentation into Go doc comments, the "Tickets
management tool" half of the spec is duplicated. This ticket removes that half,
leaving spec-erg-v1.md as a pure file-format reference: magic line, headers,
sections, grammar, closed criterion, ID convention, Postel's Law.

The culled sections (store discovery, validate rules, check, ready, close,
archive, migrate, update) are fully covered by `erg COMMAND --help` after 0090.

## Actions
1. Delete from spec-erg-v1.md: "## Tickets management tool" and all subsections.
2. Keep: Introduction (shortened), File format, Headers, Blocked-by grammar,
   Closed criterion, ID assignment, Log section, Body convention, Postel's Law.
3. Update the introduction to note that command documentation is available via
   `erg COMMAND --help` and `erg --help --all`.
4. Update the embedded base64 in bootstrap_assets.go and rebuild the binary.
5. Update AGENTS.md references if needed.

## Test
`wc -l tickets/spec-erg-v1.md` must be ≤ 150 lines after culling.
The remaining content must be sufficient to write a valid .erg file by hand.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] spec-erg-v1.md ≤ 150 lines, format-only
- [ ] No command descriptions remain in spec (validate rules, close steps, etc.)
- [ ] bootstrap_assets.go updated with new base64
- [ ] `make test` passes
